# Enforcement-surface CODEOWNERS example (L2 Governed)
# Remember:
# 1. Head-branch CODEOWNERS cannot bootstrap protection for the same PR.
# 2. Listing two owners means EITHER can satisfy CODEOWNERS, not BOTH.
#    Enforce minimum approving reviews >= 2 + require_last_push_approval +
#    dismiss_stale_reviews_on_push + no unconditional bypass in GitHub Rulesets.

/.github/workflows/ @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
/.github/CODEOWNERS @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
/.github/copilot-instructions.md @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
/Makefile @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
/AGENTS.md @org/architecture-owners
/CLAUDE.md @org/architecture-owners
/.claude/ @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
/.cursor/ @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
/.vscode/ @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
/.mcp.json @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
/skills/ @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
/scripts/ @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
/standards/ @org/architecture-owners
# Protect shared IaC/Terraform modules at the same tier as production:
/terraform/ @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
/infra/ @org/security-platform @org/architecture-owners
